  "title": "Lidl Cookie Recall 2026: FDA Warns Customers in Nine States About Undeclared Allergens",
  "summary": "Consumers Urged to Check Their Pantries After Shortbread Cookie Recall A popular imported cookie product sold at Lidl grocery stores has been recalled after federal food safety officials warned that the packaging did not properly identify certain allergens. Customers in multiple states have been advised not to eat the affected product if they have sensitivities or allergies to wheat, soy, milk, or eggs. The recall involves Eridanous Shortbread Cookies with Chocolate Truffle Coating and Apricot",
